      "worked": "The inner function $g$ has domain $[-2,2]$ and range $[0,2]$. The domain of $f$ is $(-\\infty,1]$, so the allowed inner outputs are\n$$[0,2]\\cap(-\\infty,1]=[0,1].$$\nThus the input must satisfy\n$$0\\le\\sqrt{4-x^2}\\le1.$$\nSquaring these non-negative quantities gives\n$$0\\le4-x^2\\le1.$$\nHence\n$$3\\le x^2\\le4.$$\nTherefore the domain is\n$$D=[-2,-\\sqrt{3}]\\cup[\\sqrt{3},2].$$\nOn this domain, $g$ attains every value in $[0,1]$. Since $f(t)=\\sqrt{1-t}$ decreases continuously from $f(0)=1$ to $f(1)=0$, the composition attains every value in $[0,1]$.\n$$R=[0,1].$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
